#!/home/jp/.venvs/obsws/bin/python
"""obs-macro-pad run|do <verb> [arg]|status|map — the 10-key USB pad drives the call stack (spec
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-17-obs-macro-pad.md, JP 2026-11-17 11:2x).

GNOME on Wayland delivers OBS global hotkeys only while OBS is focused, so a hotkey pad fails exactly in a meeting.
This grabs the pad exclusively (EVIOCGRAB: it stops typing into windows) and runs each key's verb itself: the stack's
own tools (`camera-scene`, `camera-mode`, `wpctl`) or an obs-websocket request. Rules from ha, the stack owner:
every OBS WRITE and every nvpoca touch runs under `flock -n ~/.local/state/camera-stack.lock` and backs off when it
is held; the program scene is never set here, only through `camera-scene brand|plain`.

  run   [--device /dev/input/eventN …] [--dry-run]   the daemon: wait for the pad, grab every interface, dispatch
  do    <verb> [arg] [--dry-run]                     one verb now (Companion, HA and tests call this)
  status                                             one line: scene, mic, camera, record, mode (reads only)
  map                                                the effective key map (and the pad's by-id name + usb id)
  find                                               the by-id event interfaces `run` would grab (nothing touched)
  serve [--bind 127.0.0.1:8765] [--dry-run]          loopback HTTP: GET /status (JSON) · POST /do/<verb>[/<arg>] — the one
                                                     OBS writer for Companion, HA and the CYD deck (same verbs, same lock).
                                                     Binds a loopback IP only; every request needs the token from
                                                     ~/.config/obs-macro-pad/token (0600) as `Authorization: Bearer <t>`
                                                     or Basic with <t> as the password; a browser Origin is refused.

Verbs: scene plain|brand · mic toggle|mute|unmute · camera toggle|hide|show · record toggle · stream toggle ·
camera-mode toggle|hdr|fast · safe · status · none.
Map: ~/.config/obs-macro-pad/map.json (or $OBS_MACRO_PAD_MAP), else the vendored default next to this file. It must
name the pad's full by-id name (up to the -event-* suffix) and its usb vendor/product: the daemon grabs only
<by-id>/<device>[-ifNN]-event-* whose ids match, and refuses (exit 2) anything else under that name.
Exit (do): 0 done · 1 not as asked · 2 usage / unknown verb · 3 OBS not answering · 4 backed off (lock held).
"""
